    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "https://codesandbox.io/s/instantsearchjs-controlled-mode-so5qw, yes this way it's way smoother. \r\n\r\n```js\r\nlet timeoutHandle;\r\n\r\nconst search = instantsearch({\r\n  indexName: 'instant_search',\r\n  searchClient,\r\n  // Try controlled mode here!\r\n  onStateChange({ uiState, setUiState }) {\r\n    console.group('onStateChange');\r\n    console.log({ uiState });\r\n    console.groupEnd();\r\n\r\n    if (timeoutHandle) {\r\n      clearTimeout(timeoutHandle);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    timeoutHandle = setTimeout(() => setUiState(uiState), 500);\r\n  },\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf we document this in the future, we need to make sure to cancel the stale updates. I don't think InstantSearch can do that out of the box.",
